      "content": "thanks for clarifying that. it seems like there's a massive gap between how the human rights groups and the state see things. \n\ni'm trying to get a sense of the academic weight here. when you say international legal experts view the Israeli defense as a way to \"deflect from reality,\" is that the dominant view in modern legal scholarship? like, is the security argument generally treated as a legitimate legal defense, or has it been largely discredited by the consensus of international law experts as being legally insufficient to justify the level of control being exercised?",
